+### Typed-origin dimensions: no standalone core cut in this packet
+
+`Framework.Physics` imports `Millennium.HolonicTypedOriginDimensions` only to re-export it; the
+facade itself refers to none of its declarations. The owner fixes `OriginAxis` to the
+length/mass/source-time/receiver-time chart and `symmetrizeDimension` to the conventional
+`Ellipse.Dim = ℤ × ℤ × ℤ`. The Einstein, stress-energy, cosmological, and primal/dual cell-measure
+dimensions are therefore instances of that chart, not a generic Physics API. The only generic
+claim in its receiver-fibre section is already available as `Foundation.TransportLift`'s
+`fibreEquivKernel`; extracting a duplicate would not add a reusable law.
+
+The stacked import graph has five paths from `Framework.Physics` to this owner: the direct
+re-export; `HolonicCosmologicalInference`; `HolonicEvolutionKinds`; `HolonicSimulationCertificate`
+then `HolonicEvolutionKinds`; and `HolonicQuantumTransport` then `HolonicEvolutionKinds`. The
+last three reach it through `HolonicFieldTheoryPassage`. Removing the direct facade import alone
+leaves four paths and does not reduce the research closure. A useful follow-up must split the
+concrete chart's consumers at the declaration boundary (including the cosmological and
+field-theory owners) before curating the facade. No core module or forwarding alias is introduced
+here.
+
